From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: the browser's blocker asked before a request goes out

setAmigaRequestBlockedHook() (AmigaNetwork.h) lets the browser say whether
a request goes out at all: GFOpenBrowser asks Tata's ad and tracker rules
(src/webcore/ob_tata.c). ResourceHandle::amigaStartRequest() asks it on the
main thread for every http request, before the cookie header and the HTTP
cache, and again for each redirect, with the page's site (the first party)
and the address. A blocked request fails as cancelled from the run loop,
after start() has returned, as a load must. With no hook set nothing
changes. The frame loader client's own check (dispatchWillSendRequest)
still counts the page's blocked loads; this one covers every load, pings
and workers' included.

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/AmigaNetwork.h b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/AmigaNetwork.h
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/AmigaNetwork.h
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/AmigaNetwork.h
@@ -82,6 +82,13 @@
 using AmigaHttpCacheHook = Function<std::unique_ptr<AmigaHttpCacheRequest>(ResourceRequest&)>;
 WEBCORE_EXPORT void setAmigaHttpCache(AmigaHttpCacheHook&&);
 
+// The browser's blocker (Tata's ad and tracker rules): whether a request goes
+// out at all. Asked on the main thread for every http request, and again for
+// each redirect, with the page's site (the first party) and the address; a
+// request it blocks fails as cancelled, after start() has returned.
+using AmigaRequestBlockedHook = bool (*)(const URL& firstParty, const URL&);
+WEBCORE_EXPORT void setAmigaRequestBlockedHook(AmigaRequestBlockedHook);
+
 // Stops the network thread, whatever it is loading; the browser calls this
 // before it exits, as an AmigaOS program does not end while a thread runs.
 WEBCORE_EXPORT void stopAmigaNetwork();
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp
@@ -71,6 +71,13 @@
     httpCacheHook() = WTF::move(hook);
 }
 
+static AmigaRequestBlockedHook requestBlockedHook;
+
+void setAmigaRequestBlockedHook(AmigaRequestBlockedHook hook)
+{
+    requestBlockedHook = hook;
+}
+
 static AmigaNetworkThreadHooks networkThreadHooks;
 
 void setAmigaNetworkThreadHooks(const AmigaNetworkThreadHooks& hooks)
@@ -114,6 +121,13 @@
 
 void ResourceHandle::amigaStartRequest(ResourceRequest&& request)
 {
+    if (requestBlockedHook && requestBlockedHook(request.firstPartyForCookies(), request.url())) {
+        RunLoop::mainSingleton().dispatch([protectedThis = Ref { *this }, url = request.url()] {
+            protectedThis->amigaDidFail(ResourceError(errorDomainWebKitInternal, 0, url, "Blocked by the browser's ad and tracker rules."_s,
+                ResourceError::Type::Cancellation));
+        });
+        return;
+    }
     appendCookieHeader(request);
     d->m_httpCache = nullptr;
     if (!std::exchange(d->m_skipHttpCache, false) && httpCacheHook())
